<p>How the panel is meant to work — designed disagreement, a chair who synthesizes without voting, an author who ratifies — is described on the <a href="{{ '/about/' | url }}">About</a> page.</p>
<p class="companion-note"><strong>Every first-person line attributed to a panelist — including the living members (Turchin, and the advisory bench) — is a reconstruction of that thinker's published positions, not a real statement they ever made.</strong> The panelists are simulations of intellectual positions (Ground Rule 16); nothing here is endorsed by any named thinker or their estate, and invented attributions to real people are prohibited (<a href="{{ '/contributing/' | url }}">CONTRIBUTING</a>). Each deliberation record carries the same disclaimer on its own page.</p>
